{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 20941961f2: the Commons cohort's register runs on a fourth Worker, dap-commons. The three existing registers stay as they are.\n\n1. Hosting. W1's hosted room is created on a new Worker, dap-commons, from a new configuration apps/room/wrangler.commons.jsonc in the BO1 head, modelled on wrangler.demo.jsonc: DEPLOYMENT dap-commons, origin https://dap-commons.inguz.workers.dev, Artifacts namespace dap-commons on the same Artifacts host, PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS equal to the ruled Commons cohort (register@23, directory@22, membership@9, rules@14, destination@16, inbox@1, commons@1), ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION unset. REGISTER_SCOPE and ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope are the same single register, as on the other Workers.\n\n2. Where the public planned register identity is bound. In that configuration file, in the same three places as dap-demo binds its register (REGISTER_SCOPE, ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope and the start configuration's register with definition platform:register@23). The head ships the file with the pins and the namespace set and the register fields holding the literal string \"unplanned\". After the head lands, the planner follows docs/deploy.md \"The order\": deploy with DEPLOYMENT and SESSION_SECRET, run dap install --plan against the new origin with --host artifacts --namespace dap-commons, set the planned ID in the configuration, redeploy, run dap install --planned, and land the configuration change as a planner follow-up with the register's public ID in its text. The W1 driver takes that configured full reference, checks that the register's definition is platform:register@23, and stops otherwise, as you proposed.\n\n3. What does not change. dap-demo, dap-grow and dap-lending keep their registers (register@17, register@17, register@5), their creation pins and their creation settings. No ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION anywhere. Nothing infers Commons for a room created under an older register; the has-commons guard and the host pre-check from ruling 7a2beda6 item 6 remain the only answer for old rooms. J4's existing-room witness and S1's rooms stay on dap-demo's register@17 and are not touched by BO1 or by the dap-commons provisioning.\n\n4. The real gap, named. New rooms are created on dap-demo, so the demo register will need Commons once BO1 is in use. That is register succession: an ordered cutoff entry in the old register and a new register under the new cohort, designed in notes/2026-10-22-definition-succession.md and not built. It is a separate item, not part of BO1. The planner files it after BO1 lands, as a design note first and then a builder slice, with dap-demo as its first witness. Until it lands, Commons rooms live on dap-commons.\n\n5. Planner-owned steps and the record. The planner creates the Artifacts namespace dap-commons, deploys the Worker, plans and installs the register, and reports the public register ID and the deployment version under the BO1 request before the W1 hosted run. Cost of this choice: a fourth Worker to deploy and keep healthy; the alternative, migrating dap-demo's register, needs succession first and would disrupt the J4 and S1 rooms. Revisit when succession lands.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}